(874, 2, '2021-07-14 14:19:05', '2021-07-14 14:19:05', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Hello everyone,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I don\'t know how much you\'ve been tracking changes on my blog. I suspect no one has, but that doesn\'t mean that I don\'t develop and work on it. There are two things I\'ve done recently you can see.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Well, actually three. But I\'ve been waiting on some things to get settled before I really start showing the third off. A sneak announcement: I have a big Vue project that\'s been done for a few months, and I\'m totally excited. It\'s not everything I would\'ve wanted to do, but it was a creative project to see what I can do. It goes with an upcoming book, is what I\'m saying, and that\'s why I\'ve been waiting on. I\'ll write a big, long post about it, how it was made and why it was made when I finally release it. However, until that time I\'ll be talking about the two things I have released.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol><li><a href=\"https://benyakiredits.com/showcase/\" data-type=\"page\" data-id=\"861\">Showcase</a> - I wanted to take some of the more cool, isolated widgets from my other projects and show them off. </li></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'My latest developments - a showcase and a backend', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '873-revision-v1', '', '', '2021-07-14 14:19:05', '2021-07-14 14:19:05', '', 873, 'https://benyakiredits.com/?p=874', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(875, 2, '2021-07-14 14:33:41', '2021-07-14 14:33:41', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Hello everyone,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I don\'t know how much you\'ve been tracking changes on my blog. I suspect no one has, but that doesn\'t mean that I don\'t develop and work on it. There are two things I\'ve done recently you can see.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Well, actually three. But I\'ve been waiting on some things to get settled before I really start showing the third off. A sneak announcement: I have a big Vue project that\'s been done for a few months, and I\'m totally excited. It\'s not everything I would\'ve wanted to do, but it was a creative project to see what I can do. It goes with an upcoming book, is what I\'m saying, and that\'s why I\'ve been waiting on. I\'ll write a big, long post about it, how it was made and why it was made when I finally release it. However, until that time I\'ll be talking about the two things I have released.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol><li><a href=\"https://benyakiredits.com/showcase/\" data-type=\"page\" data-id=\"861\">Showcase</a> - I wanted to take some of the more cool, isolated widgets from my other projects and show them off. It actually wasn\'t nearly as easy as I thought it would be to do, but I did learn a lot. That\'s been my experience, so far. Trying out something new either results in me getting frustrated and wanting to throw my computer in a lake (Machine Learning, C/C++, some parts of C#) or me learning a lot (GraphQL, Next/Nuxt, a lot of things). Now, I\'m going to talk about the process because this is a blog post. If you don\'t want the technical details, well, uh, don\'t read this post?</li></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The project is a subset of my blog\'s WordPress theme, and that may be a \'huh\' thing. A WordPress blog is composed of three things: 1. the database, 2. the theme and 3. the plugins. The database collects all of the background information that supplies this information. All the posts on a blog, for example, are in it. That I\'m the administrator is also in the database. Then there\'s a bunch of other information, but it\'s not really what you\'re going to care about. So these words, specifically are in the database. Everything else you see is part of the theme. How the menus are laid out (the actual menu items, though, is part of the database), the fonts, the designs, etc. There are some fuzzy areas where the theme decides a lot. Such as the front page, where the words that you see aren\'t coming from the database but from the theme. For example, on the portfolio page, the theme creates the cards that flip over, but the content of the cards is the database. Let\'s not talk about the plugins because, for now, it isn\'t relevant. I\'ll talk about them when I add some custom plugins.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'My latest developments - a showcase and a backend', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '873-revision-v1', '', '', '2021-07-14 14:33:41', '2021-07-14 14:33:41', '', 873, 'https://benyakiredits.com/?p=875', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(876, 2, '2021-07-14 16:10:37', '2021-07-14 16:10:37', '', 'Screen-Shot-2021-07-14-at-10.10.26-AM', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'screen-shot-2021-07-14-at-10-10-26-am', '', '', '2021-07-14 16:10:37', '2021-07-14 16:10:37', '', 873, 'https://benyakiredits.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Screen-Shot-2021-07-14-at-10.10.26-AM.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
